
  riscvsim › demo 2 · Waiting for memory                          cycle 5 of 9

     3 .data
     4 value:  .word 41
     5
     6 .text
     7 addi x5, x0, 1     # x5 = 1                            WB
     8 # lui puts 0x10000 in the upper 20 bits of x6, so x6
     9 # shows 0x10000000: the address where .data starts.
    10 lui  x6, 0x10000   # x6 = 0x10000000, where value is   MEM
  › 11 lw   x7, 0(x6)     # x7 = 41, read from memory         EX
    12 add  x10, x7, x5   # needs x7 now: one stall           ID

  ┌─ IF ────────┐┌─ ID ────────┐┌─ EX ────────┐┌─ MEM ───────┐┌─ WB ────────┐
  │ ·           ││ add x10,x7… ││ lw x7,0(x6) ││ lui x6…     ││ addi x5,x0… │
  └─────────────┘└─────────────┘└─────────────┘└─────────────┘└─────────────┘
    ✓ x5 = 1

  ! lw is reading memory. add must wait one cycle because it needs x7 from lw.
    A stall: the instruction stays where it is for a cycle, and an empty slot
    (a bubble) moves on instead.

